Document.description_en:
As part of the implementation of the Gatineau Park Sustainable Transportation Strategy, the National Capital Commission (NCC) launched a pilot program operating a shuttle service during the summer of 2022 on the Gatineau, Champlain and Lac-Fortune parkways to promote alternative means of transportation.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The continuation of this summer service requires the establishment of infrastructure to control vehicle traffic in Gatineau Park. The NCC plans to install automated gates at all Parkway entrances and exits, at six different sites, to control vehicle and shuttle traffic in the Park according to schedule.

&nbsp;

The sites are: parking lots P3, P6 (Mackenzie King Estate), P5 (intersection of the Gatineau Parkway and Kingsmere Road), P8 (intersection of the Gatineau Parkway and Meech Lake Road) and P10 (Fortune Lake Parkway), as well as the exit to Saint Raymond Boulevard.

&nbsp;

Construction will begin in the spring of 2023 and will be completed in the fall of 2023.

&nbsp;

Objectives: 

&nbsp;


	Provide a seamless shuttle service to Gatineau Park visitors in the Parkway Sector with infrastructure that will allow visitors using the shuttle to enjoy their Park experience.
	Install automated gates at strategic locations in the Park to facilitate the ingress and egress of shuttle buses and emergency vehicles on the Parkway network, while allowing the network to remain closed to unauthorized vehicles and users.
	Install signage and other traffic management measures to ensure the smooth operation of the shuttle service (e.g., dedicated stop spaces) and the safety of park users (e.g., signage indicating the presence of buses on the parkways when they are closed to motorized vehicles).


&nbsp;

The construction phases include: 

&nbsp;


	Installation of temporary signage during the construction period
	Temporary closure of traffic lanes
	Installation of automated barriers
	
		Construction of concrete bases
		Construction of electrical and communication networks
	
	
	Restoration of the sites
	Opening of lanes and activation of barriers


&nbsp;

Document.description_fr:
Dans le cadre de la mise en &oelig;uvre de la strat&eacute;gie de transport durable du parc de la Gatineau, la Commission de la capitale Nationale (CCN) a lanc&eacute; un projet-pilote de service de navette durant l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2022 sur les promenades de la Gatineau, Champlain et du Lac-Fortune afin de promouvoir des moyens de transport alternatifs.

&nbsp;

L&#39;op&eacute;ration continue de ce service estival requiert la mise en place d&#39;infrastructures pour contr&ocirc;ler la circulation de v&eacute;hicules dans le parc de la Gatineau. Pour s&#39;y faire, la CCN pr&eacute;voit installer des barri&egrave;res automatis&eacute;es &agrave; toutes les entr&eacute;es et sorties des promenades, soit 6 diff&eacute;rents sites, afin de contr&ocirc;ler la circulation des v&eacute;hicules et navettes dans le parc selon les horaires pr&eacute;vus.

&nbsp;

Les sites sont&nbsp;: les stationnements P3, P6 (Domaine Mackenzie-King), P5 (intersection de la promenade de la Gatineau et du chemin Kingsmere), P8 (intersection de la promenade de Gatineau et du chemin du lac Meech) et P10 (promenade du Lac-Fortune), ainsi que la sortie au boulevard Saint Raymond.

&nbsp;

La construction commencera au printemps 2023 et se terminera &agrave; l&#39;automne 2023.

&nbsp;

Objectifs&nbsp;: 


	Offrir un service fluide de navette aux visiteurs du parc de la Gatineau dans le secteur des promenades &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;infrastructures qui permettront aux visiteurs qui utilisent la navette d&#39;appr&eacute;cier leur exp&eacute;rience dans le parc
	Installer des barri&egrave;res automatis&eacute;es &agrave; des endroits strat&eacute;giques du parc pour faciliter l&#39;entr&eacute;e et la sortie des navettes et des v&eacute;hicules d&#39;urgence sur le r&eacute;seau des promenades tout en permettant au r&eacute;seau de demeurer ferm&eacute; aux v&eacute;hicules non-autoris&eacute;s et aux usagers non-conformes;
	Installer de la signalisation et d&#39;autres mesures de gestion de la circulation pour assurer la fluidit&eacute; du service de navette (espaces r&eacute;serv&eacute;s aux arr&ecirc;ts, etc.) et la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des usagers du parc (signalisation indiquant la pr&eacute;sence d&#39;autobus sur les promenades lorsqu&#39;elles sont ferm&eacute;es aux v&eacute;hicules motoris&eacute;s).


&nbsp;

Les phases de construction incluent : 

&nbsp;


	Installation de signalisation temporaire durant la p&eacute;riode des travaux de construction
	Fermeture temporaire de voies de circulation
	Installation des barri&egrave;res automatis&eacute;es
	
		Construction des bases de b&eacute;ton
		Construction des r&eacute;seaux &eacute;lectrique et de communication
	
	
	Remise en &eacute;tat des lieux
	Ouvertures des voies et activation des barri&egrave;res


&nbsp;

